NAME
       lsmod - list the kernel modules that are loaded

SYNOPSIS
       lsmod

DESCRIPTION
       lsmod prints the modules in the running kernel (drivers, file systems,
       firewall parts) from /proc/modules: the name, the memory it uses, and
       how many users it has and which other modules use it. modinfo NAME
       describes a module; modprobe loads or removes one.

EXAMPLES
           lsmod | grep xfs

SEE ALSO
       modprobe(8), modinfo(8)
